# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Translator Investigator — the gitignore boundary.
# The framework is shared/versioned; a dev's scope, investigations, clones, memory,
# and local surfaces are private and never leave the machine. Secrets never commit.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Per-dev scope & config  (templates/scope.yaml + templates/issue-sources.yaml ARE tracked) ──
# copied from templates/scope.yaml + templates/issue-sources.yaml by /onboard
/scope.yaml
/issue-sources.yaml

# ── Per-dev standing instructions & hooks  (AGENTS.md + .claude/settings.json ARE tracked) ─
# AGENTS.local.md = the per-dev local core (concept index + enabled-bundle snippets); the
# per-agent adapters (CLAUDE.local.md) import it. AGENTS.md itself is shared/tracked.
/AGENTS.local.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
/.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Local (unaudited) concepts — underscore-prefixed until /contribute promotes them ──
# `_<slug>.md` = a concept not yet audited/canonical (inferred|curated); local-only. /contribute
# renames it to `<slug>.md` (tracked) on promotion. Applies to global + bundle concept dirs.
**/concepts/_*.md

# ── Investigations & clones — all local & throwaway ──────────────────────────
# investigations/ includes each investigation's worktree/ (fix mode) and artifacts/; repos/ = clones
/investigations/
/repos/
# Per-dev memory lives in the agent's native store (e.g. Claude Code's harness memory). Agents
# without one fall back to a gitignored root MEMORY.md (see AGENTS.md) — ignored here so it never commits.
/MEMORY.md

# ── Extension-produced local artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────
# created only if the analysis-log extension is enabled
/analysis-log.md

# ── Enabled-bundle skill symlinks — NOT handled here (by design) ──────────────
# Shipped framework skills are tracked real dirs in .claude/skills/ with clean command
# names. Per-dev *enable* symlinks (e.g. trapi-testing) are ignored locally: `enable`
# appends each to .git/info/exclude and `disable` removes it. That keeps this committed
# file skill-agnostic (zero upkeep) and command names clean. See plan §M.

# ── Secrets (defensive — secrets must never be committed) ─────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.local.env
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*
**/secrets/

# ── Language / build cruft (from anything run at the framework root) ──────────
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── OS / editor cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
